-- ============================================================================
-- DR8 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Completion Design, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: what a completion is made of, what an API 5CT drift is,
-- how a stack up is built and what it refuses, which equipment items are wide
-- and why, and the two volumes that come from the string alone. Fourteen
-- equipment types over 49 catalog rows, every one flagged approximate. The
-- published string is 13 components and 2606.25 m, of which four runs of plain
-- tubing carry almost all the length and nine pieces of equipment carry a
-- little over thirteen metres between them.
--
-- THE FINDING THE MODULE IS BUILT ON, AND IT IS ABOUT TWO NUMBERS. Every
-- component carries an outside diameter and an inside diameter, and the two
-- answer completely different questions: the outside decides what gets DOWN
-- and appears in no volume at all, the inside decides what gets THROUGH and
-- how much the component holds. The pair does not correlate. The safety valve
-- is the widest body above the packer at 5.75 in and its bore of 2.75 in is
-- NARROWER than the plain tubing at 2.992; the perforated joint is the
-- narrowest body in the kit at 3.5 in and its bore is the full tubing bore.
-- Almost every mistake in the subject is one of those two numbers being used
-- for the other one's question.
--
-- A SECOND FINDING, IN m02. The drift deduction is a lookup on the OUTSIDE
-- diameter and on nothing else, because the mandrel sizes are standardised by
-- pipe size and a physical mandrel knows neither weight nor grade. Every
-- 9-5/8 in row in the 28 row catalog gives up the same 5/32 in, so their
-- drifts differ ONLY because their nominal bores do, which is why a drift is
-- never quoted without the weight beside it. The four classes split the
-- catalog 3 / 9 / 10 / 6, and the two casing class boundaries at 8-5/8 and
-- 13-3/8 in are INCLUSIVE at the top: no row in any real catalog sits on
-- either of them, so a classification error there survives every test written
-- from the catalog and shows up the first time somebody runs a genuine
-- boundary size.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling completionDesign module against completion_cases.json and
-- tubular_cases.json, and the teaching lab the panels and this course share is
-- pinned by completionLab.test.js across 42 cases. A numeric sweep over the
-- lessons resolved every literal carrying seven or more significant figures to
-- an engine-derived value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks
-- reports zero downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all
-- eighteen graded fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('completion', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-completion-is","title":"What a Completion Is","lesson_keys":["l01-the-last-string-in-the-well","l02-what-the-components-do","l03-two-diameters-per-component","l04-what-this-engine-models"]},{"key":"m02-api-drift","title":"API Drift","lesson_keys":["l01-an-id-is-not-what-fits","l02-the-drift-mandrel","l03-three-deduction-classes","l04-the-class-boundary","l05-drift-is-a-guarantee"]},{"key":"m03-the-stack-up","title":"The Stack-Up","lesson_keys":["l01-a-tally-is-a-telescoping-sum","l02-top-down-from-the-hanger","l03-where-the-packer-lands","l04-what-the-tally-refuses","l05-reading-a-tally"]},{"key":"m04-the-equipment","title":"The Equipment","lesson_keys":["l01-what-each-piece-is-for","l02-the-body-od-is-the-coupling-od","l03-landing-nipples-and-seat-bores","l04-the-big-body-items","l05-the-catalog-says-approx"]},{"key":"m05-volumes-and-what-a-tally-hides","title":"Volumes, and What a Tally Hides","lesson_keys":["l01-capacity-and-displacement","l02-the-steel-between-them","l03-measured-depth-not-vertical","l04-what-a-tally-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

